# Testing

## Context

Tests use vitest and live next to the code they test: `app/src/reducer.test.ts`,
`app/src/store.test.ts`, `app/src/lib/text.test.ts`. They run with
`cd app && npm test` (`vitest run`).

## Rule

- Every new action / reducer case / selector / lib function gets a test in a
  colocated `*.test.ts` file (same directory as the code under test).
- Use vitest (`describe` / `it` / `expect`) — NEVER add jest, mocha, or any
  other test framework.
- Structure each test as Arrange–Act–Assert: build the input state, perform
  one operation, assert on the result.
- Reducer tests must also assert immutability where relevant (the original
  state object is not mutated).
- Never delete or weaken existing tests to make a change pass; fix the code.

## How to verify

1. New behavior in `src/X.ts` has a matching `src/X.test.ts` change.
2. `cd app && npm test` is green (all files, no skipped tests).
3. `grep -rE "from ['\"]jest|mocha" app` — zero matches.
